.²1 To see, look at, observe, view, behold, perceive; {#drakzyasi BrAtfjAyAm#}
 <ls>Me. 10</ls>, <ls n="Me.">19</ls>; <ls>R. 3. 42</ls>.
.²2 To look upon, regard, consider; {#AtmavatsarvaBUtezu yaH paSyati sa#}
 {#paRqitaH#} <ls>Chāṇ. 5</ls>; <ls>Pt. 1. 58</ls>.
.²3 To visit, wait or call upon; {#pratyudyayO muniM drazwuM brahmARamiva#}
 {#vAsavaH#} <ls>Rām.</ls>
.²4 To perceive with the mind, learn, know, understand; {#evamAcarato dfzwvA#}
 {#Darmasya munayo gatim#} <ls>Ms. 1. 110</ls>, <ls n="Ms.">12. 23</ls>.
.²5 To inspect,

 discover.
.²6 To search, investigate, examine, decide; {#kftarakzaH samutTAya paSyedAyavyayO#}
 {#svayam#} <ls>Y. 1. 327</ls>, <ls n="Y.">2. 305</ls>.
.²7 To see by divine intuition; {#fzirdarSanAtstomAn dadarSa#} <ls>Nir.</ls>
.²8 To look helplessly on (without power to prevent what is taking place).
--{%<ab>Pass.</ab>%} ({#dfSyate#})
.²1 To be seen or perceived, become visible or manifested; {#tava taccAru#}
 {#vapurna dfSyate#} <ls>Ku. 4. 18</ls>, <ls n="Ku. 4.">3</ls>; <ls>R. 3. 40</ls>; <ls>Bk. 3. 19</ls>; {#dfzwaH svapne kitava#}
 {#ramayankAmapi tvaM mayeti#} <ls>Me. 113</ls>.
.²2 To appear or look like, seem, look; {#taTApi nIcErvinayAdadfSyata#} <ls>R. 3. 34</ls>.
.²3 To be found or seen, occur (as in a book <ab>&c.</ab>); {#dvitIyAmreqitAntezu#}
 {#tato'nyatrApi dfSyate#} <ls>Sk.</ls>; {#iti prayogo BAzye dfSyate#}.
.²4 To be considered or regarded; {#sAmAnyapratipattipUrvakamiyaM dArezu#}
 {#dfSyA tvayA#} <ls>Ś. 4. 17</ls>.

.²1 To cause any one (<ab>acc.</ab>, <ab>dat.</ab> or <ab>gen.</ab>) to see anything (<ab>acc.</ab>), to show,
 point out; {#darSaya taM cOrasiMham#} <ls>Pt. 1</ls>; {#darSayati BaktAn harim#}
 <ls>Sk.</ls>; {#pratyaBijYAnaratnaM ca rAmAyAdarSayatkftI#} <ls>R. 12. 64</ls>, <ls n="R.">1. 47</ls>, <ls n="R.">13. 24</ls>; <ls>Ms. 4. 59</ls>.
.²2 To prove, demonstrate; {#vIryaM mA na dadarSastvam#} <ls>Bk. 15. 12</ls>.
.²3 To exhibit, display, make visible; {#tadeva me darSaya deva rUpam#} <ls>Bg. 11. 45</ls>.
.²4 To produce (as in a court of justice); <ls>Ms. 8. 158</ls>.
.²5 To adduce (as evidence); {#atra SrutiM darSayati#}.
.²6 (<ab>Ā.</ab>) To show oneself, appear, show oneself or anything belonging to
 oneself; {#Bavo BaktAn darSayate#} <ls>Sk.</ls> ({%<ab>i. e.</ab>%} {#svayameva#}); {#svAM#}
 {#gfhe'pi vanitAM kaTamAsyaM hnInimIli Kalu darSayitAhe#} <ls>N. 5. 71</ls>; {#sa#}
 {#saMtataM darSayate gatasmayaH kftADipatyAmiva sADu banDutAm#} <ls>Ki. 1. 10</ls>;
 <ls>Ku. 4. 25</ls>.
